    "summary": "Scorching Dark Star, fierce The Other One, killer China>Rider",
    "blurb": "The set bursts with high‑energy gems like Hard To Handle and a soaring Dark Star, while the second half delivers relentless jams on The Other One and Attics Of My Life. Pigpen’s wild organ lifts the Lovelight jam and the band stays locked in throughout.",
    "review": "May 24, 1970 marks the Grateful Dead’s historic first UK gig at Newcastle‑Under‑Lyme, a night that still crackles with excitement. From the opening Casey Jones through a blistering Hard To Handle, Jerry Garcia rides a wave of electric intensity that peaks on an expansive Dark Star, while Phil Lesh adds vocal depth and a surprisingly full bass tone despite early mix quirks. The band’s chemistry shines in the China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue and the relentless drive of The Other One, punctuated by a seamless Attics Of My Life transition into Good Lovin'. Pigpen’s organ roars on Turn On Your Lovelight, giving the set a raw, free‑form edge. Though the board capture muddies a bit during Lovelight, the overall performance is tight, daring, and emblematic of a band on the cusp of its legendary improvisational era.",
